    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 11 slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (80.65) serving as our clear focal point; his elite 0.469 xwOBA and favorable matchup against Kumar Rocker make him the highest-floor option on the roster. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.78) also grades out as an essential start, bolstered by a significant lineup placement bump to the lead-off spot. While **Pedro Ramirez** (57.98) and **Lars Nootbaar** (60.61) carry respectable efficiency scores, our aggressive pursuit of the Stolen Base category keeps them in the mix despite facing tricky arms like Nick Lodolo and Reynaldo L\u00f3pez. We are notably cautious with **Trea Turner** (57.54) today; while he remains a priority, his matchup against Casey Mize is hampered by the pitcher's elite ability to control the running game, which slightly suppresses his overall efficiency score relative to his typical output.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Nelson Velazquez** (52.38) from the starting nine. Despite his impressive 0.407 xwOBA, the optimizer favored the positional utility of **Pedro Ramirez** and the upside of **Lars Nootbaar** in their respective platoon splits. **Nelson Velazquez** came within a fraction of a point of displacing the lower-scoring middle infielders, but the projected lineup density of the primary squad won out. We are maintaining a high alert regarding weather in two contests: **Gary Sanchez** (54.96), **Caleb Durbin** (56.07), and **Christian Yelich** (53.56) all face a heightened risk of disruption due to rain in their respective venues. With the bottom half of our lineup clustered tightly in the 50\u201355 range, any in-game weather delays or late-scratch lineup announcements for **Dillon Dingler** or **Junior Caminero** will force an immediate reassessment of our utility depth.",
